WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
Hello everybody! My name is Markiplier and, no, I am not lying when I say that.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:09.140
This baby faced gentleman that you see in front of you, is indeed, the real Markiplier.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.760
And, uh, when I'm unbearded, and I've already got a little stubble growing,

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:18.400
But when I'm unbearded, I suddenly drop back to who I was in the year 2012.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.360
And I did this on the charity live stream that we just did this weekend.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.580
And, uh, it was, it was really fun.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.240
I mean, uh, excuse also the makeup and the gold in my hair,

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.100
don't mind any of that.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.380
That's coming out for a video, uh, later this week.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:34.100
But I just wanted to take the time to say hi to you guys again.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:34.800
And...

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.500
...I don't know, I thought it was a good opportunity to kinda reintroduce myself.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.620
Because, honestly, I haven't done that in a while and

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.820
some of you may wonder why I would need to reintroduce myself.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:47.360
But I've always felt that it was important to do that

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.580
because it's very easy to become a caricature of yourself.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.120
And what I mean by that, it's very easy for people to

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:01.380
assume that they know who you are unless you keep up with that idea.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:06.320
And the idea of who you are is sometimes a very hard concept to lockdown.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.040
But I'll start with the basics.

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.300
Hi, my name is Mark.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.620
My middle name is Edward.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:13.200
My last name is Fishbach.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.680
I was born on Oahu, Hawaii in Honolulu

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:21.380
on a military base, um, to my dad and mom.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.800
Like oddly enough, that is a similar story for me as well.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.420
I was not graced upon this Earth by the gods.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.420
As some people have, uh, suspected but

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.820
Um, I'm a formal biomedical engineering student.

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:37.140
I've been doing Youtube for over five years now.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.840
And it's been an incredible ride thus far.

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:46.700
And what really brought this about is not only did I go baby face and I, I look exactly like I did back in those days.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.460
But also we watched, um, one of my old vlogs back on stream.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.760
It was for my, uh, my birthday.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.740
Oddly enough, I just turned 23, I think.

00:01:58.020 --> 00:01:58.800
And, um...

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.720
Like on that stream, I said some really silly-sounding things at the time.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.460
Er, now they do, looking back.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.720
I was talking about the statistics of the channel.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.560
And I was talking about how I decided that I wanted to be a BIG youtuber someday.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.360
When I grew up, I was gonna be a big youtuber.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:16.300
And, uh...

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:20.260
It, it was really interesting to see because at the age of 23

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:21.520
Like

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.280
I had already, like grown up.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.620
I had already grown up at that point.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.180
Or at least, I thought I did.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:27.580
Until I got to that point.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.680
Like I had worked an office job.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:32.340
I wore a tie to work everyday.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.360
And I sat in the cubicle doing engineering work.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:37.680
And I thought that was gonna be my life.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.780
And I was, I was okay with that at the time, and then I found something else

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.420
that lead me into doing Youtube.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:50.040
And I can talk about that or you can watch some videos that I've made in the past that talk about that.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.700
But long story short,

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.700
I had a medical problem.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:54.700
I had a tumor.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.200
I got that removed and that lead me to

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.680
trying to make videos for a living.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.320
And it worked, it really did.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:03.320
And...

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.640
Five years later, I have had more success than I could ever hope for.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.700
And, in the journey,

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:17.180
We've managed to build one of the greatest communities I've ever seen.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:18.060
Anywhere.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:24.600
And I am so incredibly proud of what you guys have done and I'm so incredibly--

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:29.360
Incre-incredibly proud of you guys joining us for these streams every single weekend

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:35.160
And I'm so incredibly proud of you guys continuing to champion the causes that we talk about.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:39.940
Because, it's not just about the fact that we're able to raise more money than ever before.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.200
And, and I don't know the final count from this weekend,

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.080
But I'll let you guys know as soon as I find that out.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:50.160
But it's not just about that. It's not just about us having these live streams every month

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.340
And that's the end of it.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:55.960
It's the fact that it echos beyond what we do on that day.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:00.360
Like the, the resounding success of those live streams come,

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.240
Yes, from the donations being made in the tangible good that you see out of that,

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.120
But also,

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:10.040
From how it affects other people that want to do those things.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:11.840
The ripple that it has.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:12.940
And I'm not just saying, like,

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.820
I'm not taking credit for any of this because

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:18.160
I've always said it that it's you guys that manage to do it.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:21.520
And it's the community that rallies around what we do.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:27.180
But, it's so amazing to see it ripple and continue and inspire

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:29.320
generations to come.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:35.620
To do this amazing things and to raise money for charity and go out there and try to change the world.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:46.460
And coming from the perspective of reintroducing you--myself to you guys is the idea of what I want to be when I *laughs* grow up.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.980
And that sounds like a silly thing to say, but it's true, like

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.480
What do I want to be when I grow up?

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.060
'Cause I've been doing this for five years.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.260
I'm 27 years old, which is old by some standards.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:02.840
But if you ask anyone older than me, I am still incredibly young.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:07.920
[Goofy] And it looks it right now with my baby face,

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:12.120
But I'm still incredibly young and I have so many other ambitions for what I want to do.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:17.380
And it all revolves around this incredible community that we have here.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:20.320
And I am so...

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:24.580
So excited, like everyday, I'm excited for the future.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.140
Everyday, I'm excited for what's to come.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:31.940
Everyday, I'm excited to, to, to make new challenges for myself and exceed them.

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:34.540
Or not meet them or fail and try again.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.520
But never stop creating.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.360
You know, in the endeavor.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:44.060
And that's one of the most beautiful things that I can see coming out of the community is creation.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:50.020
Like you guys going out and making things and starting your own channels and starting your own art projects.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:54.200
And finding new ways to blaze your trail and go out there.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:06:03.160
And, and, and, and I see that as just a little piece of what I did in the beginning of all this craziness.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:04.920
And I'm really happy.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.340
I don't know, I'm just really happy to be here.

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:11.460
And, and admittedly, things have been crazy on my end because

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:14.020
We've been moving offices because like we said on the stream.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.020
In case you missed it,

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:18.400
the last of it that we had, it was very nice-looking,

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:19.700
but it was horrifying.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:23.720
Like every single area in that office was horror.

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:28.280
Like there was a bug wall where bugs would just start crawling out of the walls at random.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:31.280
You never know when a centipede was about to start coming out of there.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:37.720
There was a wall that, not only flooded, but any computer equipment that you would ever put in that corner,

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:39.480
would die, inevitably.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:41.440
We went through three different computers.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.980
We resurrected a computer twice.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:48.140
And put it back in the same computer corner and it just blew up.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.160
Each and every time. It just blew up.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:56.540
We have no idea why, so it's been crazy trying to move offices to, uh, this new one that we're gonna get it set up for the next stream.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:58.560
Real nice and you're gonna see that, but...

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:00.060
Just, thank you, guys...

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:04.300
Thank you guys for holding onto the hope that...

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:07.500
...we can make the world a better place.

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:11.880
And if I had to summarize what I wanna be when I "grow up", it would be...

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:15.540
I wanna change the world.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.600
I don't just wanna make a small impact on the world.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:21.440
I wanna change the world.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:25.540
And I can't do that alone, I never could.

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.680
I never would be able to do that alone.

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:31.820
But now, in this community, I have an opportunity.

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:36.640
And I have a responsibility to guide you guys, and hopefully

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:43.580
point you guys in the right direction. And even if it comes down to the point where I am not the one who's guiding you

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:46.300
and it's you who's guiding me...

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:51.520
Then that's what it comes to. But either way, I wanna change the world.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:54.500
I wanna make a lasting impact on it.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:55.880
Hopefully, for the better by the way.

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:58.240
This is all for the better, not saying change the world for the worst.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:02.760
But change the world for the better, and make a difference.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:07.020
Today, and tomorrow, and we talked about doing this on the stream.

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:12.640
We had this idea that we'll make changes that ripple beyond our own lives.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.940
That when our times comes and goes...

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:17.640
...we'll know...

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:26.260
...that the generations that follow us will follow in our footsteps and be able to lead themselves down a path to a brighter future.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.640
And that is a beautiful idea.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.520
And that's what I want.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.000
In this silly videos that I make, and I make silly videos...

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:42.700
...comes something more profound and more amazing than I could've ever hoped for.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:46.100
So, just thank you everybody so much for watching.

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:48.540
I don't think I'm gonna keep the baby face

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.560
I, I, I do like the beard.

00:08:50.560 --> 00:08:56.960
We did it for a very specific reason that you're gonna see very soon, probably this Friday, I believe.

00:08:56.980 --> 00:09:05.900
But it's really, really, really cool to be in the middle of the most amazing time in my life.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:07.600
And I believe I'm in the middle of it.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:10.340
Because it's.. it's astonishing.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:13.540
It really is, the things that I can do now.

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:15.800
And the things that we can do together.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.160
And I'm grateful for that every single day.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:22.840
So, thank you everybody so much for watching.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.940
And as always, I will see you...

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:27.480
...in the next video.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:29.800
Buh-bye!

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:33.320
Bye, bye-bye...

